Z||000000||fierocd||08-25-2001||06:48 PM||||OK, I just finished putting in my rebuilt engine.  I got everything set and it ran fine.  When I took it out for the second test drive, it was fine till it was warmed up, then the check engine light came on and it started stalling whenever I would stop.  I was only a mile away from my house so I figured I'd go home and see what the problem was.  Half way there, I heard a loud pop,(I think it backfired) followed by a big cloud of black smoke.  I shut it off and coasted home.  When I got there I checked the codes and it came up with 33(mass air flow).  I also saw that the vaccume line going into my EGR valve came off.  My question is, can anyone tell me what the smoke was from???  Any help right now is appreciated because I only have 2 weeks to get the car fixed and then I am leaving for Texas.||||reg||5
Z||000001||btoth||08-25-2001||07:20 PM||||Check to see if your cat. is plugged up.  It will cause backfiring, stalling, and will really screw up the performance of the car and the sensors.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierocd||08-25-2001||07:26 PM||||may be a dumb question, but is there any easy way to check if your cat is clogged?  I usaully just cut them out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||08-25-2001||07:41 PM||||You may find this odd, but while I had an eng out of a jeep cherokee, dirt daubers built nests in the exh pipe while I worked on the eng.( about two months). Not likely in your case, but thought I'd share that bit of useless information. Glowing exh is an indication of clogged exh, as is poor accel.||||reg||1
